/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]writes to Spotify; that write is re-checked, journaled, reconciled,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and verified. The new private sase-org/sase-spotify plugin ships [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]with excellent docs, a strict test suite, and CI. It is installed [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and accepted end to end on athena.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]11[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]spotify_agent_access.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/spotify_agent_access.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1rs[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1rs/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Private repository and SASE project, created through a gate[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]repo[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]repo: propose creating the private sase-org/sase-spotify GitHub repo and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SASE project through a gate. After approval, verify that the repo is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]private and that its agent-chat sidecar is private or absent.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Package skeleton, shared foundation, tooling, and CI[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]scaffold[dim] · [dim][/dim]after repo[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]scaffold: build the package skeleton with every dependency declared, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]implement the shared foundation modules: paths, config, errors, the JSON[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]envelope, the UI kit, actor detection, and the SASE bridge. Add CLI [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stubs, guarded tooling, CI, and doc stubs, then set the GitHub metadata.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Setup wizard, PKCE login, and the token broker[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]auth[dim] · [dim][/dim]after scaffold[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]auth: implement the setup wizard and a PKCE login that accepts either a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]loopback callback or a pasted redirect. Add the locked, rotation-safe [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]token broker with six-month expiry tracking, plus status and logout.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Web API client, cache, library service, privacy guard, and [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]fake Spotify[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]api[dim] · [dim][/dim]after scaffold[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]api: implement the thin Web API client, with typed models for both item [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shapes, pagination, and rate-limit, quota, and budget handling. Add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshot-keyed cache, the library service with reference resolution, the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]privacy guard, and the stateful fake Spotify that every test uses.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Dashboard, playlists, podcasts, search, and doctor[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]reads[dim] · [dim][/dim]after auth, api[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reads: ship the dashboard, playlists, podcasts, search, and doctor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commands with quiet terminal output and the versioned JSON contract, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plus read-side live tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Changeset document, resolution, diffs, and preview renderers[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]changesets[dim] · [dim][/dim]after api[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]changesets: implement the changeset v1 document and its validation with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]precise errors. Add playlist and track resolution, grouping, snapshot [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pinning, diffs, the frozen-changeset store, and the plain-text, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Markdown, and terminal preview renderers.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Login-expiry watcher, reminders, and phone renewal[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]lifecycle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after auth[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lifecycle: add the scheduler job that watches login expiry and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]needs-reauth state, sends deduplicated reminders, and raises the phone [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]renewal gate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Gate-only apply executor[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]apply[dim] · [dim][/dim]after auth, changesets[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]apply: implement the gate-only executor: re-checks, journaling, chunks [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]of at most 100 URIs, reconciliation of ambiguous writes, verification, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]outcome notifications, and the drift check. Add write-side live tests [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and Spotify-semantics probes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Changeset gate, propose and history commands[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]propose[dim] · [dim][/dim]after apply, reads[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]propose: build the custom gate turn from a frozen changeset. Add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]propose, repropose, list, and show commands and the dashboard changes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]line, plus golden gate tests and an end-to-end contract test against a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real sase.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The /sase_spotify skill, README, and documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]skill-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reads, lifecycle, propose[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]skill-docs: write the /sase_spotify skill, the README, and the docs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pages, with generated terminal screenshots. Then finalize AGENTS.md and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]CONTRIBUTING.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Install on athena and end-to-end acceptance[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after skill-docs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollout: install the plugin and its skill on athena through a gate, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify the install, and request an acceptance-agent launch in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]private project for after Bryan has logged in.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1rs","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1rs.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-1rs.1"},"source_run_id":"run-f307baf665b7b4c8cc3c5bd46c860ba0","started_at":"2026-11-07T16:16:35.019445+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.10","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.11","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.5","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.6","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.7","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.8","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.9","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rs.land"]}
